            "prompt": "by doing calculations using the numbers in the table.",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\dfrac{l}{m}$ is not constant: $\\dfrac{60}{100}=0.6$ but $\\dfrac{80}{150}=\\dfrac{8}{15}$.",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{l}{m}&=\\frac{60}{100}=\\frac35\\quad\\text{for }m=100\\text{ g}\\\\\\frac{l}{m}&=\\frac{80}{150}=\\frac8{15}\\quad\\text{for }m=150\\text{ g}\\end{align*}$$\nSince $\\dfrac35\\ne\\dfrac8{15}$, the ratio $\\dfrac{l}{m}$ is not constant. Therefore the spring length is not directly proportional to the mass.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 29
          }
